            "heading": "Work Through the Crisis Framework",
            "text": "1. **Check immediate safety.** Identify whether someone needs help or the situation requires the safety process.\n2. **Gather facts before deciding.** Confirm the vehicle, location, request and known timeline.\n3. **Communicate early.** Give the manager accurate information before confusion grows around the event.\n4. **Keep the property informed.** Make sure the manager understands what is being reviewed and who owns the next step.\n5. **Collect the relevant record.** Photos, permit history, timestamps, Towbook or TowCentric activity, calls, videos and notes may all help.\n6. **Resolve verified company mistakes professionally.** Use the authorized decision and resolution process.\n7. **Record serious concerns neutrally.** Document threats, harassment, lawsuits and escalations as reported or observed facts.\n8. **Follow through to closure.** Keep the manager updated until the issue is resolved and the required follow-up is complete.\n\nEach step reduces guesswork for the next person. A complete timeline is more useful than a strong opinion delivered before the record is checked."
